Package: plainpy
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: fasm, gcc, curl
Description: small Python: an interpreter and a compiler of typed programs
 plainpy runs Python programs with nothing but the C library: a full Python
 3.14 parser, a bytecode interpreter and a standard library written in
 Python (json, re, datetime, logging, unittest, asyncio, threading,
 http.server, zipfile, tomllib and more), all in three files.
 .
 plainpy --compile compiles statically typed programs to small native
 executables: Linux i386 and KolibriOS through fasm (no linker, no libc, no
 runtime library to install). plainpy add / sync take pure-Python packages
 from PyPI (through curl) and check which of them compiled programs may use.
